        // Create second proposal using newGrantProposal (both increment proposalCount)
        c.newGrantProposal(address(0x2), 100);
        // At this point: reference: proposalCount = 2, buggy: proposalCount = 1
        // Now call cancelProposal(old=1, new=2). For this to succeed in reference:
        // - mapPID_finalising[1] must be true -> we need to finalise proposal 1 first
        // - new proposal (2) must have minority (not required here? The require checks hasMinority on newProposalID (2), so need that false? It says "Must have minority" meaning true? Actually require(hasMinority(newProposalID), ...) -> requires minority true (votes > totalWeight/6). Since no one voted, votes=0, so hasMinority returns false, causing revert.
